---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Steward
    participant Profile as Profile page<br/>components/ProfilePage.tsx
    participant Action as API route<br/>PATCH /api/profile<br/>app/api/profile/route.ts
    participant Auth as Supabase Auth
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL

    Note over Steward,DB: Covers US 1.0.2.

    Steward->>Profile: Open own profile and select Edit profile
    activate Profile
    Note right of Profile: Edit profile button shows only when isOwner<br/>(people.auth_user_id = session user) (AT1).
    Steward->>Profile: Change display name, skills, focus areas or contact (socials)
    Steward->>Profile: Select Save changes
    Profile->>Profile: Display name is not empty and at most 29 characters<br/>(input required, maxLength 29) (AT3)

    alt Display name is empty
        Profile-->>Steward: Browser blocks save on the required field (AT3)
    else Display name is filled
        Profile->>Action: saveProfile(): fetch PATCH /api/profile<br/>{displayName, skills, focusAreas, socials}
        activate Action
        Action->>Auth: getUser() from the session cookie
        activate Auth
        Auth-->>Action: Signed-in user id or no user
        deactivate Auth
        Note right of Action: Body has no user id. The write uses the session client<br/>(not the service role), so RLS "users update only their<br/>own person record" and the column grant stop other writes.

        alt No session
            Action-->>Profile: 401 'Sign in to edit your profile.'
            Profile-->>Steward: Show error
        else Signed in
            Action->>Action: Check again on server (AT3): display name 1 to 29 characters,<br/>at most 12 tags of 1 to 40 characters, normaliseSocials
            alt Body or values not valid
                Action-->>Profile: 400 {error: message}
                Profile-->>Steward: Show the error message
            else Values are valid
                Action->>DB: UPDATE people SET display_name, skills, focus_areas<br/>WHERE auth_user_id = session user
                activate DB
                alt people update failed
                    DB-->>Action: Error
                    Action-->>Profile: 500 'Unable to save your profile.'
                    Profile-->>Steward: Show error and keep the typed values
                else No people row for session user
                    DB-->>Action: No row
                    Action-->>Profile: 404 'Profile not found.'
                    Profile-->>Steward: Show error
                else people row updated
                    DB-->>Action: Saved people row
                    opt socials sent
                        Action->>DB: UPSERT socials (person_id) ON CONFLICT person_id
                        alt socials upsert failed
                            DB-->>Action: Error
                            Action-->>Profile: 500 'Unable to save your contact details.'<br/>(people already saved)
                            Profile-->>Steward: Show error and keep the typed values
                        end
                    end
                    Action-->>Profile: Saved profile
                    Profile-->>Steward: Show new values, skills and focus areas (AT4, AT6)
                end
                deactivate DB
            end
        end
        deactivate Action
    end
    deactivate Profile

    Note over Steward,DB: Values are read from the database on each load. After sign out and sign in,<br/>the profile shows the saved values (AT5). A missing table (42P01) returns 503.<br/>socials.email is a contact field. The sign-in email is not edited here.
